  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform the input grid by filling the interior of every rectangular border of 1s.\n    The fill value is 2 if the interior area (height-2)*(width-2) is even,\n    otherwise 7.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    # Work on a copy so original 1s are preserved\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] != 1:\n                continue\n            # Check if this cell is the top\u2011left corner of a rectangle:\n            # no 1 above and no 1 to the left.\n            if (i > 0 and grid[i-1][j] == 1) or (j > 0 and grid[i][j-1] == 1):\n                continue\n\n            # Determine width of the top side\n            w = 0\n            while j + w < cols and grid[i][j+w] == 1:\n                w += 1\n            # Determine height of the left side\n            h = 0\n            while i + h < rows and grid[i+h][j] == 1:\n                h += 1\n\n            # We need at least a 3x3 shape to have an interior\n            if w < 3 or h < 3:\n                continue\n\n            # Verify the bottom side\n            valid = True\n            bottom = i + h - 1\n            for k in range(j, j + w):\n                if grid[bottom][k] != 1:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                continue\n\n            # Verify the right side\n            right = j + w - 1\n            for k in range(i, i + h):\n                if grid[k][right] != 1:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                continue\n\n            # Compute fill value based on parity of interior area\n            interior_area = (h - 2) * (w - 2)\n            fill_val = 2 if interior_area % 2 == 0 else 7\n\n            # Fill the interior cells that are not part of a border (i.e., not 1)\n            for r in range(i + 1, i + h - 1):\n                for c in range(j + 1, j + w - 1):\n                    if out[r][c] != 1:   # preserve existing borders (including nested ones)\n                        out[r][c] = fill_val\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform the input grid by filling the interior of every rectangular border of 1s.\n    The fill value is 2 if the interior area (height-2)*(width-2) is even,\n    otherwise 7.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    # Work on a copy so original 1s are preserved\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    for i in range(rows):\n        for j in range(cols):\n            if grid[i][j] != 1:\n                continue\n            # Check if this cell is the top\u2011left corner of a rectangle:\n            # no 1 above and no 1 to the left.\n            if (i > 0 and grid[i-1][j] == 1) or (j > 0 and grid[i][j-1] == 1):\n                continue\n\n            # Determine width of the top side\n            w = 0\n            while j + w < cols and grid[i][j+w] == 1:\n                w += 1\n            # Determine height of the left side\n            h = 0\n            while i + h < rows and grid[i+h][j] == 1:\n                h += 1\n\n            # We need at least a 3x3 shape to have an interior\n            if w < 3 or h < 3:\n                continue\n\n            # Verify the bottom side\n            valid = True\n            bottom = i + h - 1\n            for k in range(j, j + w):\n                if grid[bottom][k] != 1:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                continue\n\n            # Verify the right side\n            right = j + w - 1\n            for k in range(i, i + h):\n                if grid[k][right] != 1:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if not valid:\n                continue\n\n            # Compute fill value based on parity of interior area\n            interior_area = (h - 2) * (w - 2)\n            fill_val = 2 if interior_area % 2 == 0 else 7\n\n            # Fill the interior cells that are not part of a border (i.e., not 1)\n            for r in range(i + 1, i + h - 1):\n                for c in range(j + 1, j + w - 1):\n                    if out[r][c] != 1:   # preserve existing borders (including nested ones)\n                        out[r][c] = fill_val\n    return out",
